==English==
{{rfc|the fourth verb sense "trait of a dog" is defined like a noun - should it be reworded, or moved to the noun section / the entry "backbiter"?}}
===Alternative forms===
* [[back-bite]]
===Etymology===
[[back]] + [[bite]]

{{attention|en|fifth sense is unneeded?}}
===Verb===
{{en-verb|backbites|backbiting|backbit|backbitten}}

# To make [[spiteful]] [[slanderous]] or [[defamatory]] [[statement]]s about someone.
# {{informal}} To attack from behind or when out of [[earshot]].
# To speak badly of an [[absent]] individual.
# A [[trait]] of a [[shy]], mean, dog.
# To act as mean as a '''back-biting''' dog.

